{"id":110777524166638,"type":"artist","name":"Thin White Rope","artist":null,"year":1984,"weight":10,"info":{"tags":["desert rock","Paisley Underground","rock","indie rock","alternative rock"],"country":"US","begin":"1984","end":"1992","kind":"Group","similar":["The Dream Syndicate","Rain Parade","Green on Red","The Long Ryders","Eleventh Dream Day","Game Theory","The Three O'Clock","Buffalo Tom","Steve Wynn","True West"],"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/TWR_davis_WEF_4x6.jpg?width=500","bio":"Thin White Rope was an American rock band fronted by Guy Kyser and related to the desert rock and paisley underground sub-genres. The band released five albums to critical acclaim.\n\nOver time, formed in Davis, United States in 1984, the band retained on singer-songwriter and guitarist Guy Kyser and guitarist Roger Kunkel, with a changing lineup of drummers and bass guitarists. It was noted for its twin guitar attack (compare Television), innovative use of feedback structures and oblique lyrics."},"works":[{"id":19438066321678,"type":"album","name":"Exploring The Axis","artist":"Thin White Rope","year":1985,"weight":16,"yt":"o0AUQgmHM2Y","src":"books,charts,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","rank":757,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":206252946483818,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Paisley Underground","rank":11,"scaruffi":7.0},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":123,"scaruffi":7.0}],"n_lists":3}},{"id":196864045459595,"type":"album","name":"Moonhead","artist":"Thin White Rope","year":1987,"weight":5,"yt":"EO0tffO-p2w","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":206252946483818,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Paisley Underground","rank":15,"scaruffi":null},{"id":161051722508702,"name":"RYM Top — Rock — Jangle Pop","rank":148,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":186759852964967,"type":